# BookDrop Strategic Roadmap (decision recorded 2026-05-05)

## Why this file exists

Future sessions kept relitigating the same architecture question: should BookDrop be a standalone product or a sub-feature of an existing parent app? Founder's decision (2026-05-05): **standalone V1 launch first → if no traction, fold as a sub-option in an existing product as a beta probe → if probe shows demand, spin out cleanly.** This file records the path so it isn't relitigated every session.

---

## The 3-stage path

### Stage 1 — Standalone V1 launch (current)
**Goal:** ship BookDrop as its own product at its own URL with everything tested, audited, performing.

**Scope:**
- BookDrop in its own repo with its own deploy pipeline
- BookDrop on its own domain (or `*.vercel.app` for V1)
- Marketing positions BookDrop as a standalone bookkeeper / CPA product
- Pricing: Free / Starter $39/mo / Pro $79/mo (existing tiers)

**Gate to advance to Stage 2:** ALL of:
- [ ] V1 deployed to production (cloud mode, not demo)
- [ ] Database migrations run on the live project
- [ ] Email provider wired, real reminder email sent
- [ ] Stripe products created, real checkout completed for at least one tier
- [ ] All tests passing, build clean, no console errors
- [ ] Mobile responsive verified at 375px width
- [ ] **AI-first audit passed** (`.claude/rules/ai-first-principles.md` §2 — at least 3/5 PASS, no critical FAIL). Current verdict per `DATA_FLYWHEEL.md` is 1/5 PASS → pivot work is mandatory before launch.
- [ ] **Pre-launch bug checklist run** (`.claude/rules/bug-checklist.md` — all 13 patterns)
- [ ] **Off-platform backup pipeline live** (`scripts/backup-pg-to-r2.ps1`), first backup verified
- [ ] First quarterly restore drill scheduled (within 30 days of going live)
- [ ] At least one paying customer or 5 beta CPAs actively using it for >30 days

### Stage 2 — Beta probe inside an existing product (only if Stage 1 traction is weak)
**Trigger:** Stage 1 launches but acquisition / conversion is below threshold (say, <10 paying customers in 90 days post-launch).

**Goal:** measure CPA market signal cheaply by leveraging an adjacent product's existing user base. The probe is a sales/distribution experiment, not an architectural fold-in.

**Scope:**
- Add a "I'm a bookkeeper / CPA" sign-up option to an adjacent product's signup page that deep-links to BookDrop
- BookDrop remains its own codebase, its own deploy, its own database
- Cross-product auth via shared `auth.users.id` only (if adjacent product is Supabase-backed); never a hard FK from BookDrop tables into the parent product's tables
- BookDrop continues to operate at its own URL with its own brand

**Architectural constraints to preserve spin-out optionality** (enforce these in Stage 1 already so Stage 3 stays cheap):
- Keep BookDrop's schema fully isolated. If sharing a database project, prefix every table (`bookdrop_*`) and never hard-FK into a non-BookDrop table.
- Document the data shape end-to-end so an "export BookDrop → standalone Postgres" script is feasible later.
- Marketing pages stay at separate URLs even during the probe (don't merge landing pages).

**Gate to advance to Stage 3:** ANY of:
- 25+ active practitioners signing up via the probe in 60 days
- $500+ MRR from probe signups in 90 days
- Strong qualitative signal: 5+ unsolicited "I'd pay more for this" or "I want to refer my colleagues" messages

**Or kill if:** <5 signups in 60 days AND no paying customers from the probe.

### Stage 3 — Spin out cleanly OR keep folded
Decision based on Stage 2 signal:

**If signal is strong → spin out:**
- Register the final brand domain (verify availability, don't assume)
- Migrate BookDrop's schema to its own Postgres project (the Stage 1+2 isolation constraints make this cheap)
- Migrate existing customers via API + email confirmation
- BookDrop's marketing site goes live at the new domain
- BookDrop becomes its own business with its own customer base, support, brand

**If signal is weak → kill or fold:**
- If <5 signups: shut down BookDrop, archive the repo, reclaim the dev time
- If 5-25 signups but no paying conversion: keep as a sub-feature in the adjacent product, no separate marketing, no separate brand
- Document the lesson in `errors-fixed.json` (failed-pivot category) and `lessons.md`

